# Copy to .env (git-ignored). Everything here is optional EXCEPT
# E2E_DATABASE_URL on a machine whose tourney-api/.env points at hosted
# Postgres — which is most of them.
#
# This suite is destructive: global-setup wipes every e2e-% tournament, user
# and invitation, then the specs create real rows. It must have a database of
# its own. Both the test process (helpers/env.ts) and the API process
# (scripts/run-api.sh) read this value, and both refuse to start if it does
# not resolve to localhost or 127.0.0.1.
#
#   createdb tourney_e2e
#   cd ../tourney-api && DATABASE_URL=... go run ./cmd/migrate up && go run ./cmd/seed
#
E2E_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/tourney_e2e?sslmode=disable

# Only if this database was seeded with different accounts than tourney-api/.env
# names. Sign-in is invitation-only OTP, so each address needs a matching
# accepted invitation — cmd/seed creates both.
# SEED_ORGANIZER_EMAIL=organizer@laga.test
# SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@laga.test
